@startuml
title Matrix + Keycloak Demo — Logical Stack
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam nodesep 24
skinparam ranksep 30

actor "Users\nweb / native client / export admin" as Users
rectangle "Nginx reverse proxy\nElement Web + public HTTPS/WSS routes" as Edge

package "Routed through Nginx" {
  rectangle "Keycloak + MAS\nidentity endpoints" as Identity
  rectangle "Synapse\nMatrix API; admin API private" as Synapse
  rectangle "Export Service\nauthenticated scoped ZIP API" as Export
}

package "Private service network" {
  rectangle "Provisioner\nidentity + session issuer" as Provisioner
  rectangle "Policy Sync\nreads grants; manages rooms" as PolicySync
  rectangle "OrgBot\nPL 0 E2EE client" as OrgBot
}

Users --> Edge
Edge --> Identity : sign-in
Edge --> Synapse : Matrix API
Edge --> Export : authenticated export API
Provisioner --> Identity : private account / session setup
Identity --> PolicySync : roles / groups
PolicySync --> Synapse : room policy
Synapse <--> OrgBot : E2EE events + keys
Export --> OrgBot : exact authorized room scope

note right of Provisioner
  Admin-token volume: Provisioner writes;
  Policy Sync reads read-only. OrgBot has no
  mount of this volume.
end note

note right of OrgBot
  Separate session volume: Provisioner writes;
  OrgBot mounts read-only. Crypto store is private.
  Synapse relays E2EE events and keys; it does not
  decrypt room content. Export receives only the
  Bot's observed/decrypted ZIP, which may be partial.
end note

note bottom
  Optional MatrixRTC authorization and signaling
  are shown separately in matrixrtc-call.puml.
end note
@enduml
